WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:08.700
Perfect Pair, from Team Code Reapers. Developed by Joel Tomy and Jay Malhotra, with Esteban Shen, Chuyu Xu and Jou-En (Zoe) Tsai.

2
00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:15.240
Every refund ends a sale. Perfect Pair is an AI returns desk that keeps the customer, and the margin.

3
00:00:15.590 --> 00:00:23.650
Maya's boots are too tight. In seconds, the agent checks her photo, reads the reviews, and finds the fix: a size 8 wide.

4
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:32.870
She sees simple options: a free exchange, or Smart Credit with an in-store bonus and discounts on slow-moving stock. A return becomes a sale.

5
00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:38.290
On the same five returns, it keeps 3.8× the value of a rules engine.

6
00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:44.670
Anything risky goes to a store associate or manager, with a policy assistant to help them decide.

7
00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:51.990
In a simulated pilot, refunds fall, exchanges and store credit rise, and the margin saved roughly doubles.

8
00:00:52.340 --> 00:00:58.370
And as it learns, it settles more returns on its own, so store teams can focus on what matters most.

9
00:00:58.720 --> 00:01:02.300
Refunds end relationships. Exchanges continue them.
